    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1449">

                <pb facs="1405" n="1395" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1395"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">026 China/8–1649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-16T15:00:00+08:00">August 16, 1949—3
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 16—12:57 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 959. Chen Li-fu,<anchor n="61" xml:id="d1449-f1"/> as might be expected,
                    was vitriolic on White Paper. He complained bitterly that when Marshall was here
                    he saw only Communists and sought only understand Communist points of view,
                    ignoring Kmt elder statesmen. He, Chen, had had only one discussion with
                    Marshall. Yu Yu-jen,<anchor n="62" xml:id="d1449-f2"/> Yu Ta-wei<anchor n="63"
                        xml:id="d1449-f3"/> and Chu Chia-hua had fared likewise, he said. Ire from
                    reactionary elements in Kmt <pb facs="1406" n="1396" xml:id="pg1396"/> over
                    White Paper is of course to be expected. Word comes to me from Chiang
                        Monlin,<anchor n="64" xml:id="d1449-f4"/> however, who discussed matter with
                    Generalissimo in Taipei and quotes Generalissimo as saying lightly: “I suppose
                    they had to get it out of their system.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1449-f1" n="61" xml:id="d1449-f1-content">
                <p>Chinese Minister without Portfolio.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1449-f2" n="62" xml:id="d1449-f2-content">
                <p>President of the Chinese Control Yuan.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1449-f3" n="63" xml:id="d1449-f3-content">
                <p>Then Chinese Minister of Communications.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1449-f4" n="64" xml:id="d1449-f4-content">
                <p>Chairman of Chinese Rehabilitation Affairs Commission.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
